2-D FOUNDATION: emergent depth vs required receptive field (2-D conv stack + global max-pool)
G=12x12 k=3, 8 seeds x 3 restarts, up to L=4. two spikes at diagonal separation s.
RF >= s+1 per axis needed => depth >= s/2. accuracy should be chance until L covers the pair.

  sep s (need L) | mean test acc at depth L=1..4      | spread(SD) at each L
  s=2 (need L=1)   | 0.665 0.856 0.728 0.628   | 0.01 0.04 0.11 0.07
  s=4 (need L=2)   | 0.635 0.687 0.681 0.710   | 0.02 0.06 0.05 0.08
  s=6 (need L=3)   | 0.602 0.589 0.541 0.545   | 0.03 0.02 0.05 0.03

stable if the lift-off depth tracks s (chance until ~L=s/2) with modest spread across seeds.
this is a REPLICATION check, not a new claim -- the foundation for a 2-D reuse/recombine study.
